      "message": "As an FYI, I am about to delete the built-in crop rects stored directly on SkImageFilter_Base. The factories will still take crop rects as a convenience, but everything is moving to being handled by `SkCropImageFilter`. Internally, for blurs and matrix convolutions a non-decal SkTileMode and a provided crop rect map to a chain of filters: crop w/ tile mode -\u003e blur/convolve -\u003e crop w/ decal. This uses the same crop geometry to define where the repeat/clamping starts and the limit of the final output.\n\nIt hasn\u0027t been a priority, but I plan on exposing `SkImageFilters::Crop` publicly to allow you to compose separate input and output crops and tile modes around other image filters. Since you\u0027re a module, you can experiment early by including `src/effects/imagefilters/SkCropImageFilter.h` and calling `SkMakeCropImageFilter(...)`.",
      "revId": "f2f2533ab9be778572271237dfe5a947445f5139",
